#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# reals

#% text
# `reals` is the domain of the real numbers, for facts `element(x, reals)` in `assuming` and `refine`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `element(x, reals)` with a number `x` is decided at once: `true` or `false`. With a symbol it is a fact that `assuming` adds to the assumptions.

#% item
# Functions that use assumptions (`simplify`, `refine`, `power_expand` and the sign tests) take the domain into account.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
element(pi, reals)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
element(-2.5, reals)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
element(im, reals)
#% output
#= false

#% cell
element(1 + im, reals)
#% output
#= false

#% text
# A symbol in the domain:

#% cell
assuming(element(x, reals), simplify(sqrt(x^2)))
#% output
#= abs(x)

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
assuming(element(x, reals), is_nonnegative(x^2))
#% output
#= true

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# A symbol alone is not decided:

#% cell
element(x, reals)
#% output
#= element(x, reals)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `element`, `assuming`, `refine`, `complexes`, `rationals`
